IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- s 2(1): the defined terms about PERSONS, CORPORATIONS and the people who act for them: advocate and solicitor, auditor,
-- chairperson, chief executive officer, executive officer, entity, connected person, customer, franchise, principal,
-- representative, and every term the Act hands to another Act (company, corporation, director, officer, related corporation ...)
-- or to the Second Schedule (dealing in capital markets products ...).
-- Imports prelude and daydate only.
--
-- How to read a function in this module.
--   Every defined term of s 2(1) is ONE function, named `s 2(1) "<term>" <the thing> is <the term>`, over the facts a person could state.
--   The result is MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--     JUST TRUE   the thing is within the term (a limb of the definition is met and no exclusion applies);
--     JUST FALSE  the TEXT says it is not: a definition that says "means" and no limb is met, or an express exclusion ("but does not include");
--     NOTHING     the text does not say: an "includes" definition (an open list) with no listed limb met.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--   Every branch that answers "no" carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "..."`; every branch that
--   answers "not covered" carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`.
--   A limb the Act hands to the Authority, the regulations or another Act ("prescribed", "specified", "as defined in the
--   Banking Act 1970") is an INPUT named for the fact ("the Authority has prescribed ..."), never a thing read from memory.
--   The definitions apply "unless the context otherwise requires" (the chapeau of s 2(1)): that qualification is
--   `s 2(1) the definitions apply unless the context otherwise requires` in sfa-definitions-rest.l4, not repeated here.

§ `s 2(1): persons and corporations`

-- src:1758 | “advocate and solicitor” means an advocate and solicitor of the
-- src:1759 | Supreme Court or a foreign lawyer as defined in section 2(1)
-- src:1760 | of the Legal Profession Act 1966;
@ref s 2(1) "advocate and solicitor" (src:1758-1760)
GIVEN
    `the person is an advocate and solicitor of the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an advocate and solicitor of the Supreme Court?
    `the person is a foreign lawyer as defined in section 2(1) of the Legal Profession Act 1966` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a foreign lawyer as section 2(1) of the Legal Profession Act 1966 defines the term?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "advocate and solicitor" the person is an advocate and solicitor` MEANS
    IF `the person is an advocate and solicitor of the Supreme Court` OR `the person is a foreign lawyer as defined in section 2(1) of the Legal Profession Act 1966`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an advocate and solicitor of the Supreme Court or a foreign lawyer as defined in section 2(1) of the Legal Profession Act 1966"

-- src:1782 | “auditor” means a public accountant who is registered or
-- src:1783 | deemed to be registered under the Accountants Act 2004 and,
-- src:1784 | in Division 1 of Part 13, when used in relation to an entity not
-- src:1785 | being a company, includes —
-- src:1787 | (a) a person who is duly registered, licensed, approved or
-- src:1788 | otherwise authorised to practise as an auditor (such
-- src:1789 | practice to include the issue of any opinion, report or
-- src:1790 | other document on the audit of any financial
-- src:1791 | statement) —
-- src:1793 | (i) under the laws of the place where the entity is
-- src:1794 | formed or constituted; or
-- src:1796 | (ii) under the laws of the place of his or her
-- src:1797 | practice, if the auditing standards that are or
-- src:1798 | will be applied to the financial statements of the
-- src:1799 | entity are —
-- src:1801 | (A) auditing standards commonly applied in
-- src:1802 | that place; or
-- src:1804 | (B) international auditing standards (by
-- src:1805 | whatever name called); or
-- src:1807 | (b) such other person as the Authority may approve in
-- src:1808 | any particular case to be an auditor for such entity;
@ref s 2(1) "auditor" (src:1782-1808)
GIVEN
    `the person is a public accountant registered or deemed to be registered under the Accountants Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a public accountant registered, or deemed to be registered, under the Accountants Act 2004?
    `the provision being read is in Division 1 of Part 13 and the entity is not a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you reading the word "auditor" in Division 1 of Part 13, in relation to an entity that is not a company?
    `the person is duly registered, licensed, approved or otherwise authorised to practise as an auditor under the laws of the place where the entity is formed or constituted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person duly registered, licensed, approved or otherwise authorised to practise as an auditor (including issuing opinions and reports on the audit of financial statements) under the laws of the place where the entity is formed or constituted?
    `the person is so authorised under the laws of the place of the person's practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person so authorised under the laws of the place of the person's own practice?
    `the auditing standards applied to the entity's financial statements are those commonly applied in that place of practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the auditing standards that are or will be applied to the entity's financial statements auditing standards commonly applied in that place of practice?
    `the auditing standards applied to the entity's financial statements are international auditing standards, by whatever name called` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the auditing standards that are or will be applied to the entity's financial statements international auditing standards, by whatever name called?
    `the Authority has approved the person in this case to be an auditor for the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority approved the person, in this particular case, to be an auditor for the entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "auditor" the person is an auditor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a public accountant registered or deemed to be registered under the Accountants Act 2004`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the provision being read is in Division 1 of Part 13 and the entity is not a company` AND (`the person is duly registered, licensed, approved or otherwise authorised to practise as an auditor under the laws of the place where the entity is formed or constituted` OR (`the person is so authorised under the laws of the place of the person's practice` AND (`the auditing standards applied to the entity's financial statements are those commonly applied in that place of practice` OR `the auditing standards applied to the entity's financial statements are international auditing standards, by whatever name called`)) OR `the Authority has approved the person in this case to be an auditor for the entity`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the provision being read is in Division 1 of Part 13 and the entity is not a company`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): in Division 1 of Part 13, for an entity that is not a company, "auditor" "includes" the persons in (a) and (b), a list that is not closed
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a public accountant who is registered or deemed to be registered under the Accountants Act 2004"

-- src:1872 | “chairperson” means a chairperson of a board of directors;
@ref s 2(1) "chairperson" (src:1872-1872)
GIVEN
    `the person is a chairperson of a board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a chairperson of a board of directors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "chairperson" the person is a chairperson` MEANS
    IF `the person is a chairperson of a board of directors`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a chairperson of a board of directors"

-- src:1874 | “chief executive officer”, in relation to an approved exchange, a
-- src:1875 | recognised market operator, a licensed trade repository, a
-- src:1876 | licensed foreign trade repository, an approved clearing house,
-- src:1877 | a recognised clearing house, an approved holding company,
-- src:1878 | the holder of a capital markets services licence, an authorised
-- src:1879 | benchmark administrator, an authorised benchmark
-- src:1880 | submitter, a designated benchmark submitter or any other
-- src:1881 | corporation (called in this definition a relevant person) means
-- src:1882 | any person, by whatever name called, who is —
-- src:1884 | (a) in the direct employment of, or acting for or by
-- src:1885 | arrangement with, the relevant person; and
-- src:1887 | (b) principally responsible for the management and
-- src:1888 | conduct of the business of the relevant person in
-- src:1889 | Singapore;
@ref s 2(1) "chief executive officer" (src:1874-1889)
GIVEN
    `the relevant person is an approved exchange, recognised market operator, licensed trade repository, licensed foreign trade repository, approved clearing house, recognised clearing house, approved holding company, holder of a capital markets services licence, authorised benchmark administrator, authorised benchmark submitter, designated benchmark submitter or any other corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the relevant person one of the bodies the definition lists, or any other corporation?
    `the person is in the direct employment of, or acting for or by arrangement with, the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person in the direct employment of, or acting for, or by arrangement with, the relevant person (by whatever name called)?
    `the person is principally responsible for the management and conduct of the business of the relevant person in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person principally responsible for the management and conduct of the relevant person's business in Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "chief executive officer" the person is a chief executive officer of the relevant person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the relevant person is an approved exchange, recognised market operator, licensed trade repository, licensed foreign trade repository, approved clearing house, recognised clearing house, approved holding company, holder of a capital markets services licence, authorised benchmark administrator, authorised benchmark submitter, designated benchmark submitter or any other corporation`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to an approved exchange, ... or any other corporation (called in this definition a relevant person)"; a relevant person that is none of these is not covered
        IF `the person is in the direct employment of, or acting for or by arrangement with, the relevant person` AND `the person is principally responsible for the management and conduct of the business of the relevant person in Singapore`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any person, by whatever name called, who is (a) in the direct employment of, or acting for or by arrangement with, the relevant person; and (b) principally responsible for the management and conduct of the business of the relevant person in Singapore"

-- src:2458 | “executive officer”, in relation to an approved exchange, a
-- src:2459 | recognised market operator, a licensed trade repository, a
-- src:2460 | licensed foreign trade repository, an approved clearing house,
-- src:2461 | a recognised clearing house, an approved holding company,
-- src:2462 | the holder of a capital markets services licence, an authorised
-- src:2463 | benchmark administrator, an authorised benchmark
-- src:2464 | submitter, a designated benchmark submitter or any other
-- src:2465 | corporation (called in this definition a relevant person),
-- src:2466 | means any person, by whatever name called, who is —
-- src:2468 | (a) in the direct employment of, or acting for or by
-- src:2469 | arrangement with, the relevant person; and
-- src:2471 | (b) concerned with or takes part in the management of
-- src:2472 | the relevant person on a day‑to‑day basis;
@ref s 2(1) "executive officer" (src:2458-2472)
GIVEN
    `the relevant person is an approved exchange, recognised market operator, licensed trade repository, licensed foreign trade repository, approved clearing house, recognised clearing house, approved holding company, holder of a capital markets services licence, authorised benchmark administrator, authorised benchmark submitter, designated benchmark submitter or any other corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the relevant person one of the bodies the definition lists, or any other corporation?
    `the person is in the direct employment of, or acting for or by arrangement with, the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person in the direct employment of, or acting for, or by arrangement with, the relevant person (by whatever name called)?
    `the person is concerned with or takes part in the management of the relevant person on a day-to-day basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned with, or does the person take part in, the management of the relevant person on a day-to-day basis?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "executive officer" the person is an executive officer of the relevant person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the relevant person is an approved exchange, recognised market operator, licensed trade repository, licensed foreign trade repository, approved clearing house, recognised clearing house, approved holding company, holder of a capital markets services licence, authorised benchmark administrator, authorised benchmark submitter, designated benchmark submitter or any other corporation`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to an approved exchange, ... or any other corporation (called in this definition a relevant person)"; a relevant person that is none of these is not covered
        IF `the person is in the direct employment of, or acting for or by arrangement with, the relevant person` AND `the person is concerned with or takes part in the management of the relevant person on a day-to-day basis`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any person, by whatever name called, who is (a) in the direct employment of, or acting for or by arrangement with, the relevant person; and (b) concerned with or takes part in the management of the relevant person on a day-to-day basis"

