-- src:2829 | Second Schedule;
@ref s 2(1) "providing credit rating services" (src:2828-2829)
GIVEN
    `the activity meets the Second Schedule meaning of providing credit rating services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the activity meet the meaning of "providing credit rating services" that the Second Schedule gives?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "providing credit rating services" the activity is providing credit rating services` MEANS
    IF `the activity meets the Second Schedule meaning of providing credit rating services`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has the meaning given in the Second Schedule"

