@ref s 2(1) "providing custodial services" (src:2831-2832)
GIVEN
    `the activity meets the Second Schedule meaning of providing custodial services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the activity meet the meaning of "providing custodial services" that the Second Schedule gives?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "providing custodial services" the activity is providing custodial services` MEANS
    IF `the activity meets the Second Schedule meaning of providing custodial services`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has the meaning given in the Second Schedule"

-- src:2921 | “regulated activity” means an activity specified in the
-- src:2922 | Second Schedule;
