`s 2(1) "regulated activity" the activity is a regulated activity` MEANS
    IF `the activity is one specified in the Second Schedule`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an activity specified in the Second Schedule"

-- s 2(1) "entity": what the Act lists and what it excludes, over the core's `Kind of entity`.

-- src:2419 | “entity” includes a corporation, an unincorporated association, a
-- src:2420 | partnership and the government of any state, but does not
-- src:2421 | include a trust;
@ref s 2(1) "entity" (src:2419-2421)
GIVEN
    `the kind of body` IS A `Kind of entity` @desc What kind of body is it: a corporation, an unincorporated association, a partnership, the government of a state, a trust, or some other body?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "entity" the body is an entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of body`
    WHEN `a trust` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include a trust"
    WHEN `a corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an unincorporated association` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a partnership` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the government of a state` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `some other body` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "entity includes a corporation, an unincorporated association, a partnership and the government of any state" lists without closing the list

-- s 2(1) "connected person": (a) in relation to an individual, (b) in relation to a firm, limited liability partnership or corporation.
-- Control of "not less than 20% of the voting power" is asked as the votes controlled and the total votes (so the boundary is exact).

-- src:2226 | “connected person”, in relation to —
-- src:2228 | (a) an individual, means —
-- src:2230 | (i) the individual’s spouse, son, adopted son,
-- src:2231 | stepson, daughter, adopted daughter,
-- src:2232 | stepdaughter, father, stepfather, mother,
-- src:2233 | stepmother, brother, stepbrother, sister or
-- src:2234 | stepsister; and
-- src:2236 | (ii) a firm, a limited liability partnership or a
-- src:2237 | corporation in which the individual or any of
-- src:2238 | the persons mentioned in sub‑paragraph (i) has
-- src:2239 | control of not less than 20% of the voting
-- src:2240 | power in the firm, limited liability partnership
-- src:2241 | or corporation, whether such control is
-- src:2242 | exercised individually or jointly; or
-- src:2244 | (b) a firm, a limited liability partnership or a corporation,
-- src:2245 | means another firm, limited liability partnership or
-- src:2246 | corporation in which the firstmentioned firm, limited
-- src:2247 | liability partnership or corporation has control of not
-- src:2248 | less than 20% of the voting power in that other firm,
-- src:2249 | limited liability partnership or corporation,
-- src:2254 | and a reference in this Act to a person connected to another
-- src:2255 | person is to be construed accordingly;
@ref s 2(1) "connected person" (src:2226-2255)
GIVEN
    `the relation of the person to the individual` IS A `Family relation` @desc How is the person related to the individual: spouse, son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter, stepdaughter, father, stepfather, mother, stepmother, brother, stepbrother, sister, stepsister, or some other relation?
    `the person is a firm, a limited liability partnership or a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a firm, a limited liability partnership or a corporation?
    `the voting power in that body controlled by the individual or any of those relatives, individually or jointly` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the voting power in that firm, limited liability partnership or corporation do the individual and the relatives listed above control, individually or jointly (in votes)?
    `the total voting power in that body` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total voting power in that firm, limited liability partnership or corporation (in votes)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "connected person" (a) the person is connected to the individual` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the relation of the person to the individual` EQUALS `some other relation`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is a firm, a limited liability partnership or a corporation` AND `the voting power in that body controlled by the individual or any of those relatives, individually or jointly` AT LEAST (`the total voting power in that body` TIMES 20%)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means (i) the individual's spouse, son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter, stepdaughter, father, stepfather, mother, stepmother, brother, stepbrother, sister or stepsister; and (ii) a firm, a limited liability partnership or a corporation in which the individual or any of the persons mentioned in sub-paragraph (i) has control of not less than 20% of the voting power"

GIVEN
    `the first body has control, individually or jointly, of voting power in the other body (in votes)` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the voting power in the other firm, limited liability partnership or corporation does the first one control, individually or jointly (in votes)?
    `the total voting power in the other body` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total voting power in the other firm, limited liability partnership or corporation (in votes)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "connected person" (b) the body is connected to the firm, limited liability partnership or corporation` MEANS
    IF `the first body has control, individually or jointly, of voting power in the other body (in votes)` AT LEAST (`the total voting power in the other body` TIMES 20%)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) a firm, a limited liability partnership or a corporation, means another firm, limited liability partnership or corporation in which the firstmentioned firm, limited liability partnership or corporation has control of not less than 20% of the voting power"

-- s 2(1) "customer": the Act gives a different meaning for each group of Parts.
DECLARE `s 2(1) "customer" provision read` IS ONE OF
    `s 2(1) "customer" of a licence holder, for Parts 4, 6, 7 and 15`
    `s 2(1) "customer" of a licence holder, for Part 5`
    `s 2(1) "customer" for Part 3 and the definition of user`
    `s 2(1) "customer" for any other provision`

-- src:2264 | “customer” means —
-- src:2266 | (a) in relation to a holder of a capital markets services
-- src:2267 | licence —
-- src:2269 | (i) for the purposes of Parts 4, 6, 7 and 15, a person
-- src:2270 | on whose behalf the holder carries on or will
-- src:2271 | carry on any regulated activity; or
-- src:2273 | (ii) for the purposes of Part 5 —
-- src:2275 | (A) a person on whose behalf the holder
-- src:2276 | carries on or will carry on any regulated
-- src:2277 | activity; or
-- src:2279 | (B) any other person with whom the holder,
-- src:2280 | as principal, enters or will enter into
-- src:2281 | transactions for the sale or purchase of
-- src:2282 | capital markets products,
-- src:2284 | (ii) but does not include such person or class of
-- src:2285 | persons as may be prescribed for the purposes
-- src:2286 | of this sub‑paragraph; or
-- src:2288 | (b) for the purposes of Part 3 and the definition of “user”,
-- src:2289 | a person on whose behalf a member of an approved
-- src:2290 | exchange, an approved clearing house, a recognised
-- src:2291 | clearing house or a recognised market operator (as
-- src:2292 | the case may be) carries on any activity regulated
-- src:2293 | under this Act, but does not include —
-- src:2295 | (i) the member, with respect to dealings for the
-- src:2296 | member’s own account;
-- src:2301 | (ii) any officer, director, employee or
-- src:2302 | representative of the member; or
-- src:2304 | (iii) a related corporation of the member, with
-- src:2305 | respect to accepted instructions to deal for an
-- src:2306 | account belonging to, and maintained wholly
-- src:2307 | for the benefit of, that related corporation;
@ref s 2(1) "customer" (src:2264-2307)
GIVEN
    `the provision being read` IS A `s 2(1) "customer" provision read` @desc Which provision is the word "customer" being read for: Parts 4, 6, 7 and 15 (a licence holder's customer), Part 5 (a licence holder's customer), Part 3 or the definition of "user", or any other provision?
    `the holder of a capital markets services licence carries on or will carry on a regulated activity on behalf of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the holder of a capital markets services licence carry on, or will it carry on, a regulated activity on behalf of the person?
    `the holder enters or will enter, as principal, into transactions with the person for the sale or purchase of capital markets products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the holder, as principal, enter or will it enter into transactions with the person for the sale or purchase of capital markets products?
    `the person is one the regulations prescribe not to be a customer for Part 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person one (or of a class) that is prescribed not to be a customer for the purposes of Part 5?
    `a member of an approved exchange, approved clearing house, recognised clearing house or recognised market operator carries on an activity regulated under this Act on behalf of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a member of an approved exchange, approved clearing house, recognised clearing house or recognised market operator carry on an activity regulated under this Act on behalf of the person?
    `the person is the member itself, dealing for the member's own account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the member itself, in respect of dealings for the member's own account?
    `the person is an officer, director, employee or representative of the member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an officer, director, employee or representative of the member?
    `the person is a related corporation of the member, in respect of accepted instructions to deal for an account belonging to, and maintained wholly for the benefit of, that related corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a related corporation of the member, in respect of instructions accepted to deal for an account belonging to, and maintained wholly for the benefit of, that related corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "customer" the person is a customer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision being read`
    WHEN `s 2(1) "customer" of a licence holder, for Parts 4, 6, 7 and 15`
        THEN IF `the holder of a capital markets services licence carries on or will carry on a regulated activity on behalf of the person`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) in relation to a holder of a capital markets services licence (i) for the purposes of Parts 4, 6, 7 and 15, a person on whose behalf the holder carries on or will carry on any regulated activity"
    WHEN `s 2(1) "customer" of a licence holder, for Part 5`
        THEN IF `the person is one the regulations prescribe not to be a customer for Part 5`
             THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include such person or class of persons as may be prescribed for the purposes of this sub-paragraph"
             ELSE IF `the holder of a capital markets services licence carries on or will carry on a regulated activity on behalf of the person` OR `the holder enters or will enter, as principal, into transactions with the person for the sale or purchase of capital markets products`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) for the purposes of Part 5 (A) a person on whose behalf the holder carries on or will carry on any regulated activity; or (B) any other person with whom the holder, as principal, enters or will enter into transactions for the sale or purchase of capital markets products"
    WHEN `s 2(1) "customer" for Part 3 and the definition of user`
        THEN IF `the person is the member itself, dealing for the member's own account` OR `the person is an officer, director, employee or representative of the member` OR `the person is a related corporation of the member, in respect of accepted instructions to deal for an account belonging to, and maintained wholly for the benefit of, that related corporation`
             THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include (i) the member, with respect to dealings for the member's own account; (ii) any officer, director, employee or representative of the member; or (iii) a related corporation of the member, with respect to accepted instructions to deal for an account belonging to, and maintained wholly for the benefit of, that related corporation"
             ELSE IF `a member of an approved exchange, approved clearing house, recognised clearing house or recognised market operator carries on an activity regulated under this Act on behalf of the person`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) for the purposes of Part 3 and the definition of user, a person on whose behalf a member of an approved exchange, an approved clearing house, a recognised clearing house or a recognised market operator (as the case may be) carries on any activity regulated under this Act"
    WHEN `s 2(1) "customer" for any other provision`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the definition gives a meaning only for Parts 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 15 and the definition of user

-- src:2561 | “franchise” means a written agreement or arrangement between
-- src:2562 | 2 or more persons by which —
-- src:2564 | (a) a party (called in this definition the franchisor) to the
-- src:2565 | agreement or arrangement authorises or permits
-- src:2566 | another party (called in this definition the
-- src:2567 | franchisee), or a person associated with the
-- src:2568 | franchisee, to exercise the right to engage in the
-- src:2569 | business of offering, selling or distributing goods or
-- src:2570 | services in Singapore under a plan or system
-- src:2571 | controlled by the franchisor or a person associated
-- src:2572 | with the franchisor;
-- src:2574 | (b) the business carried on by the franchisee or the
-- src:2575 | person associated with the franchisee (as the case
-- src:2576 | may be) is capable of being identified by the public as
-- src:2577 | being substantially associated with a trade or service
-- src:2578 | mark, logo, symbol or name identifying, commonly
-- src:2583 | connected with or controlled by the franchisor or a
-- src:2584 | person associated with the franchisor;
-- src:2586 | (c) the franchisor exerts, or has authority to exert, a
-- src:2587 | significant degree of control over the method or
-- src:2588 | manner of operation of the franchisee’s business;
-- src:2590 | (d) the franchisee or a person associated with the
-- src:2591 | franchisee is required under the agreement or
-- src:2592 | arrangement to make payment or give some other
-- src:2593 | form of consideration to the franchisor or a person
-- src:2594 | associated with the franchisor; and
-- src:2596 | (e) the franchisor agrees to communicate to the
-- src:2597 | franchisee, or a person associated with the
-- src:2598 | franchisee, knowledge, experience, expertise,
-- src:2599 | know‑how, trade secrets or other information
-- src:2600 | whether or not it is proprietary or confidential;
@ref s 2(1) "franchise" (src:2561-2600)
GIVEN
    `the agreement or arrangement is in writing and between 2 or more persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement or arrangement written, and between two or more persons?
    `the franchisor authorises or permits the franchisee, or a person associated with the franchisee, to engage in the business of offering, selling or distributing goods or services in Singapore under a plan or system controlled by the franchisor or a person associated with the franchisor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a party (the franchisor) authorise or permit another party (the franchisee), or a person associated with the franchisee, to exercise the right to engage in the business of offering, selling or distributing goods or services in Singapore under a plan or system controlled by the franchisor or a person associated with the franchisor?
    `the business carried on by the franchisee is capable of being identified by the public as substantially associated with a trade or service mark, logo, symbol or name identifying, commonly connected with or controlled by the franchisor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the franchisee's business capable of being identified by the public as substantially associated with a trade or service mark, logo, symbol or name that identifies, or is commonly connected with or controlled by, the franchisor or a person associated with the franchisor?
    `the franchisor exerts, or has authority to exert, a significant degree of control over the method or manner of operation of the franchisee's business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the franchisor exert, or have authority to exert, a significant degree of control over the method or manner of operation of the franchisee's business?
    `the franchisee, or a person associated with the franchisee, is required to make payment or give some other form of consideration to the franchisor or a person associated with the franchisor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the franchisee (or a person associated with the franchisee) required under the agreement or arrangement to make payment or give some other form of consideration to the franchisor or a person associated with the franchisor?
    `the franchisor agrees to communicate knowledge, experience, expertise, know-how, trade secrets or other information to the franchisee or a person associated with the franchisee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the franchisor agree to communicate knowledge, experience, expertise, know-how, trade secrets or other information (proprietary or confidential or not) to the franchisee or a person associated with the franchisee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "franchise" the agreement or arrangement is a franchise` MEANS
    IF `the agreement or arrangement is in writing and between 2 or more persons` AND `the franchisor authorises or permits the franchisee, or a person associated with the franchisee, to engage in the business of offering, selling or distributing goods or services in Singapore under a plan or system controlled by the franchisor or a person associated with the franchisor` AND `the business carried on by the franchisee is capable of being identified by the public as substantially associated with a trade or service mark, logo, symbol or name identifying, commonly connected with or controlled by the franchisor` AND `the franchisor exerts, or has authority to exert, a significant degree of control over the method or manner of operation of the franchisee's business` AND `the franchisee, or a person associated with the franchisee, is required to make payment or give some other form of consideration to the franchisor or a person associated with the franchisor` AND `the franchisor agrees to communicate knowledge, experience, expertise, know-how, trade secrets or other information to the franchisee or a person associated with the franchisee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a written agreement or arrangement between 2 or more persons by which (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; (d) ...; and (e) ..."

-- src:2816 | “principal”, in relation to a representative, means a person
-- src:2817 | whom the representative is in the direct employment of, is
-- src:2818 | acting for or is acting by arrangement with, and on behalf of
-- src:2819 | whom the representative carries or will carry out any
-- src:2820 | regulated activity;
@ref s 2(1) "principal" (src:2816-2820)
GIVEN
    `the representative is in the direct employment of, is acting for, or is acting by arrangement with, the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the representative in the direct employment of, acting for, or acting by arrangement with, the person?
    `the representative carries or will carry out a regulated activity on behalf of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the representative carry out, or will the representative carry out, a regulated activity on behalf of the person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "principal" the person is the principal of the representative` MEANS
    IF `the representative is in the direct employment of, is acting for, or is acting by arrangement with, the person` AND `the representative carries or will carry out a regulated activity on behalf of the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a representative, means a person whom the representative is in the direct employment of, is acting for or is acting by arrangement with, and on behalf of whom the representative carries or will carry out any regulated activity"

-- s 2(1) "representative": three meanings, by what the principal is.
DECLARE `s 2(1) "representative" the principal is` IS ONE OF
    `s 2(1) "representative" a person who carries on business in a regulated activity`
    `s 2(1) "representative" an authorised or exempt benchmark administrator`
    `s 2(1) "representative" an authorised, exempt or designated benchmark submitter`

-- src:2977 | “representative” —
-- src:2979 | (a) in relation to a person (A) who carries on business in
-- src:2980 | any regulated activity, except for the purposes of
-- src:2981 | Part 13 and except as otherwise provided for in
-- src:2982 | paragraphs (b) and (c) —
-- src:2984 | (i) means a person (B), by whatever name called,
-- src:2985 | in the direct employment of, or acting for, or by
-- src:2986 | arrangement with A, who carries out for A any
-- src:2987 | regulated activity (other than work ordinarily
-- src:2988 | performed by accountants, clerks or cashiers),
-- src:2989 | whether or not B is remunerated, and whether
-- src:2990 | B’s remuneration (if any) is by way of salary,
-- src:2991 | wages, commission or otherwise; and
-- src:2993 | (ii) includes, where A is a corporation, any officer
-- src:2994 | of A who performs for A any regulated activity,
-- src:2995 | whether or not the officer is remunerated, and
-- src:2996 | whether the officer’s remuneration (if any) is
-- src:2997 | by way of salary, wages, commission or
-- src:2998 | otherwise;
-- src:3000 | (b) in relation to a person (C) that is an authorised
-- src:3001 | benchmark administrator or an exempt benchmark
-- src:3002 | administrator —
-- src:3004 | (i) means a person (D), by whatever name called,
-- src:3005 | in the direct employment of, or acting for, or by
-- src:3006 | arrangement with C, who carries out the
-- src:3007 | activity of administering a designated
-- src:3008 | benchmark (other than work ordinarily
-- src:3009 | performed by accountants, clerks or cashiers),
-- src:3010 | whether or not D is remunerated, and whether
-- src:3011 | D’s remuneration (if any) is by way of salary,
-- src:3012 | wages, commission or otherwise; and
-- src:3017 | (ii) includes, where C is a corporation, any officer
-- src:3018 | of C who performs for C the activity of
-- src:3019 | administering a designated benchmark,
-- src:3020 | whether or not the officer is remunerated, and
-- src:3021 | whether the officer’s remuneration (if any) is
-- src:3022 | by way of salary, wages, commission or
-- src:3023 | otherwise; and
-- src:3025 | (c) in relation to a person (E) that is an authorised
-- src:3026 | benchmark submitter, an exempt benchmark
-- src:3027 | submitter or a designated benchmark submitter —
-- src:3029 | (i) means a person (F), by whatever name called,
-- src:3030 | in the direct employment of, or acting for, or by
-- src:3031 | arrangement with E, who carries out the
-- src:3032 | activity of providing information in relation
-- src:3033 | to a designated benchmark (other than work
-- src:3034 | ordinarily performed by accountants, clerks or
-- src:3035 | cashiers), whether or not F is remunerated, and
-- src:3036 | whether F’s remuneration (if any) is by way of
-- src:3037 | salary, wages, commission or otherwise; and
-- src:3039 | (ii) includes, where E is a corporation, any officer
-- src:3040 | of E who performs for E the activity of
-- src:3041 | providing information in relation to a
-- src:3042 | designated benchmark, whether or not the
-- src:3043 | officer is remunerated, and whether the
-- src:3044 | officer’s remuneration (if any) is by way of
-- src:3045 | salary, wages, commission or otherwise;
@ref s 2(1) "representative" (src:2977-3045)
GIVEN
    `what the principal is` IS A `s 2(1) "representative" the principal is` @desc What is the principal: a person who carries on business in a regulated activity, an authorised or exempt benchmark administrator, or an authorised, exempt or designated benchmark submitter?
    `the provision being read is in Part 13` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you reading the word "representative" in Part 13?
    `the person, by whatever name called, is in the direct employment of, or acting for, or by arrangement with, the principal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person (by whatever name called) in the direct employment of, or acting for, or by arrangement with, the principal?
    `the person carries out for the principal the activity that goes with that kind of principal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person carry out for the principal the activity that goes with it: any regulated activity (for a person carrying on business in a regulated activity), administering a designated benchmark (for a benchmark administrator), or providing information in relation to a designated benchmark (for a benchmark submitter)?
    `the work is work ordinarily performed by accountants, clerks or cashiers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the work work ordinarily performed by accountants, clerks or cashiers?
    `the principal is a corporation and the person is an officer of it who performs the activity for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the principal a corporation, and is the person an officer of it who performs that activity for it (whether or not the officer is remunerated)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "representative" the person is a representative of the principal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `what the principal is` EQUALS `s 2(1) "representative" a person who carries on business in a regulated activity` AND `the provision being read is in Part 13`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except for the purposes of Part 13"; the definition gives no meaning there
        IF (`the person, by whatever name called, is in the direct employment of, or acting for, or by arrangement with, the principal` AND `the person carries out for the principal the activity that goes with that kind of principal` AND (NOT `the work is work ordinarily performed by accountants, clerks or cashiers`)) OR (`the principal is a corporation and the person is an officer of it who performs the activity for it` AND `the person carries out for the principal the activity that goes with that kind of principal`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) in relation to a person (A) who carries on business in any regulated activity ... (i) means a person (B), by whatever name called, in the direct employment of, or acting for, or by arrangement with A, who carries out for A any regulated activity (other than work ordinarily performed by accountants, clerks or cashiers) ...; and (ii) includes, where A is a corporation, any officer of A who performs for A any regulated activity"

-- src:1762 | “appointed representative”, in respect of a type of regulated
-- src:1763 | activity, has the meaning given by section 99D, and
-- src:1768 | “appointed representative” means an appointed
-- src:1769 | representative in respect of any type of regulated activity;
@ref s 2(1) "appointed representative" (src:1762-1769)
GIVEN
    `the person is an appointed representative in respect of that type of regulated activity within section 99D` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an appointed representative in respect of that type of regulated activity, as section 99D gives the meaning?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "appointed representative" (a) the person is an appointed representative in respect of a type of regulated activity` MEANS
    IF `the person is an appointed representative in respect of that type of regulated activity within section 99D`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in respect of a type of regulated activity, has the meaning given by section 99D"

GIVEN
